---
/**
 * Runtime authorization decision flow with DENY termination,
 * blocking-obligation fulfilment, and an explicit re-evaluation return path.
 * Presentation-only — does not alter RA01 decision or obligation semantics.
 */
interface Props {
  label?: string;
}

const { label = 'Runtime authorization decision flow' } = Astro.props;
const titleId = 'runtime-authorization-flow-title';
---

<figure class="arch-flow authz-runtime" aria-labelledby={titleId} id="runtime-authorization-flow">
  <div class="authz-runtime__header">
    <p class="authz-runtime__eyebrow">Runtime sequence</p>
    <h3 id={titleId} class="authz-runtime__title">{label}</h3>
    <p class="authz-runtime__lead">
      How one authorization decision executes: interception, evaluation, enforcement, blocking
      obligations with re-evaluation, then domain validity checks before the protected action.
    </p>
  </div>

  <ol class="authz-runtime__trunk">
    <li class="authz-runtime__node">
      <span class="authz-runtime__box">Consumer — protected action intent</span>
      <span class="authz-runtime__arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
    </li>
    <li class="authz-runtime__node">
      <span class="authz-runtime__box">
        PEP — intercepts protected action
        <span class="authz-runtime__hint"
          >Requests a decision and enforces the outcome. Does not evaluate policy.</span
        >
      </span>
      <span class="authz-runtime__arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
    </li>
    <li class="authz-runtime__node">
      <span class="authz-runtime__box">Authorization request</span>
      <span class="authz-runtime__arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
    </li>
    <li class="authz-runtime__node" id="runtime-evaluation">
      <span class="authz-runtime__box authz-runtime__box--emphasis">
        PDP — policy evaluation
        <span class="authz-runtime__hint"
          >Evaluates assigned authority, trusted authorization context and published policy. May
          consume relevant domain information via PIP / projection. Does not execute authentication,
          approval workflows, business transactions or domain invariants.</span
        >
      </span>
      <span class="authz-runtime__arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
    </li>
    <li class="authz-runtime__node">
      <span class="authz-runtime__box">
        Decision response
        <span class="authz-runtime__hint"
          >ALLOW | DENY · Reason · Obligations · References / validity context</span
        >
      </span>
      <span class="authz-runtime__arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
    </li>
    <li class="authz-runtime__node">
      <span class="authz-runtime__box">
        PEP — interpret and enforce
        <span class="authz-runtime__hint"
          >Applies the returned decision and any blocking obligations. Prevents unauthorized
          continuation.</span
        >
      </span>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="authz-runtime__branches" role="group" aria-label="Decision branches after PEP enforcement">
    <div class="authz-runtime__branch authz-runtime__branch--deny">
      <p class="authz-runtime__branch-title">DENY — terminal</p>
      <p class="authz-runtime__branch-text">
        The protected-action path ends. Execution does not continue and does not re-enter the flow.
        A DENY is not converted into progression by step-up or approval; those outcomes appear only
        when returned as obligations on an ALLOW path.
      </p>
      <span class="authz-runtime__box authz-runtime__box--terminal">Reject / stop</span>
    </div>

    <div class="authz-runtime__branch authz-runtime__branch--allow" id="blocking-obligations">
      <p class="authz-runtime__branch-title">ALLOW</p>
      <div class="authz-runtime__split">
        <div class="authz-runtime__path">
          <p class="authz-runtime__path-label">Blocking obligation unmet</p>
          <p class="authz-runtime__path-intro">
            Illustrative blocking obligations include STEP_UP, REQUIRE_APPROVAL and
            REQUIRE_SECOND_AUTHORIZER. Fulfilment is coordinated by the responsible capability — it
            is not itself final authorization.
          </p>
          <ol class="authz-runtime__path-steps">
            <li>Do not permit the protected action yet</li>
            <li>PEP coordinates obligation fulfilment by the responsible capability</li>
            <li>Failed or incomplete fulfilment cannot reach the protected action</li>
            <li>
              If fulfilment materially changes authorization context →
              <a href="#runtime-evaluation">return to PDP evaluation</a>
            </li>
          </ol>
          <div class="authz-runtime__return" aria-label="Return path to evaluation">
            <span class="authz-runtime__box authz-runtime__box--loop"
              >Re-evaluate — new decision for PEP</span
            >
            <span class="authz-runtime__return-connector" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="authz-runtime__return-label">return to evaluation</span>
              <span class="authz-runtime__return-arrow">↑</span>
            </span>
            <p class="authz-runtime__return-note">
              Satisfying an obligation does not automatically become ALLOW. The PDP re-evaluates and
              returns a new decision for the PEP to enforce — which may still be DENY, ALLOW with
              further obligations, or effective ALLOW.
            </p>
            <a class="authz-runtime__return-link" href="#runtime-evaluation"
              >Return to PDP evaluation</a
            >
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="authz-runtime__path authz-runtime__path--continue">
          <p class="authz-runtime__path-label">
            Effective ALLOW — blocking obligations satisfied; decision validity preserved
          </p>
          <p class="authz-runtime__path-intro">
            Enterprise authorization established authority to attempt. Domain checks still decide
            whether the action is valid.
          </p>
          <ol class="authz-runtime__path-steps">
            <li>Domain authorization</li>
            <li>Domain invariant checks (may still prevent execution)</li>
            <li>Protected action</li>
          </ol>
          <span class="authz-runtime__box authz-runtime__box--result">Protected action</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ul class="authz-runtime__rules">
    <li>
      Decision taxonomy remains <strong>ALLOW | DENY</strong>. Reasons and obligations stay distinct.
    </li>
    <li>DENY is terminal for the protected-action path.</li>
    <li>ALLOW with an unmet blocking obligation does not permit execution.</li>
    <li>
      Obligation fulfilment is not final authorization — re-evaluation may still DENY or impose
      further obligations.
    </li>
    <li>
      Only an effective ALLOW with required blocking obligations satisfied and applicable decision
      validity preserved may continue to domain checks.
    </li>
    <li>
      Authority to attempt (enterprise authorization) is not the same as validity of action (domain
      authorization / invariants).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <figcaption class="authz-runtime__caption">
    Consumer intent is intercepted by the PEP, which requests a PDP evaluation of assigned
    authority, trusted context and published policy. DENY terminates. ALLOW with unmet blocking
    obligations blocks continuation until fulfilment; context change returns to PDP evaluation for a
    new decision enforced by the PEP. Effective ALLOW continues to domain authorization and
    invariants, which may still prevent the protected action.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
